"""
main_gui.py -- START HERE. This is the app: run this file to launch
Plassys Shadow Simulator.

    python3 main_gui.py

Built with PySide6 (Qt): a menu bar, an icon-only toolbar (the icon IS
the button, no text label -- hover to see what it does), dockable/
tabbed side panels, and a central matplotlib canvas shared by every
tab. Dark-themed by default (see parametric_junction_view.BG_COLOR and
friends for the palette), with a light mode available from the View
menu.

This module owns the whole user interface -- every tab (Design,
Deposition Angles & Shadow Simulation, Recipe, Measure Resistance,
Interpret Results), the Front Page, and the window chrome around all
of them. Every other file in this project is a plain, framework-
agnostic Python module (geometry, recipe logic, data models, analysis
math) that this file imports and wires up to widgets; none of them
depend on Qt themselves, so they can be understood, tested, or reused
independently of the GUI. See README.md for what each of those modules
does and a tour of every tab.
"""

